diff --git a/ralph/progress.txt b/ralph/progress.txt
index 630991e7516c3512eb2a9d58b619aabff641447e..3327c5ff1f3e684eef998b9aebd16c99f09f16fc
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Usage reconciliation lives at the metering boundary: inspect append-only `usage_events` window metadata, replay counters through `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents`, rely on `usage_counter_adjustments` for closed-period late usage idempotency, and record low-confidence gaps/quarantines/resets as value-free operator drift findings until a dedicated usage-drift taxonomy exists.
 - Metered overage hooks run at the usage-counter aggregation boundary, not inside quota/resource mutation code: runtime entitlement resolution carries plan/subscription metadata, `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents` stamps `usage_counters` with `entitlement_key`, `overage_policy_mode`, `overage_decision`, included/overage quantities, and an audit event, and `BillingExportRepository.Prepare` snapshots those fields into `billing_export_items` so provider adapters can bill/review overages without changing quota code.
 - Production operations command artifacts should follow the same static-release-gate pattern as Kubernetes/systemd artifacts: keep `deploy/operations/<command>.sh`, `deploy/operations/README.md`, `cmd/yalla-api`/`cmd/yalla-worker` entrypoint support, SECURITY.md, CI, `scripts/verify.sh`, and `internal/release/*_static_test.go` in lockstep; dry-run paths must work without production secrets and print only redacted environment names.
 - Single-node systemd operations artifacts should follow the same static-release-gate pattern as Kubernetes artifacts: keep `deploy/systemd/yalla-api.service`, `deploy/systemd/yalla-worker.service`, `deploy/systemd/README.md`, `deploy/systemd/control-plane.env.example`, SECURITY.md, CI, and `scripts/verify.sh` in lockstep; load secrets only from `/etc/yalla/control-plane.env`; preserve separate API/worker units, non-root `User=yalla`, systemd hardening, journald structured logs, API `/healthz` + `/readyz`, and worker no-HTTP-listener health semantics.
@@ -38680,3 +38681,38 @@
   - `plan_entitlements.metadata` already carries `overage_behavior`; preserve it through `SubscriptionRepository.ResolveEntitlements` when runtime code needs pricing metadata.
   - Billing export items should snapshot overage fields from frozen counters so provider retries keep the same billing/review basis even if counters are replayed later.
 ---
+## 2026-05-19 14:43:57 +03 - BE-0580
+- What was implemented
+  - Added `metering.UsageReconciler`, a store-backed usage reconciliation worker service that replays one organization/period through `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents`.
+  - Added validation for tenant, period, aggregation version, expected metric streams, and quarantined sample metadata.
+  - Added detection for missing metric windows, overlapping duplicate windows, counter resets via safe metadata counters, and quarantined source samples.
+  - Added low-confidence discrepancy recording as tenant-scoped `drift_findings` with request/correlation ids, while using the existing closed-period adjustment logic for late usage without double-counting.
+- Files changed
+  - `internal/controlplane/metering/usage_reconciliation.go`
